1
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:07,257
<i>You're an actor, aren't you?</i>

2
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:09,134
<i>I'm the actor and performer,</i>

3
00:00:09,217 --> 00:00:11,678
Konta Hoshino.

4
00:00:11,761 --> 00:00:15,223
I heard from Midori
that you're mainly working as an extra.

5
00:00:15,306 --> 00:00:19,144
Well, extras live as the character too,
so they are actors. Just so you know.

6
00:00:19,227 --> 00:00:21,980
You were just lazing around
at our parents' house.

7
00:00:22,063 --> 00:00:24,357
<i>The three of us</i>
<i>actually post videos online.</i>

8
00:00:24,441 --> 00:00:26,651
<i>Would you consider appearing in one?</i>

9
00:00:26,735 --> 00:00:28,153
Hey.

10
00:00:28,236 --> 00:00:30,280
This guy is an actor.

11
00:00:30,363 --> 00:00:32,032
Oh, the video from the other day?

12
00:00:32,115 --> 00:00:33,241
They actually uploaded it.

13
00:00:33,324 --> 00:00:34,826
Hey, look at the channel name.

14
00:00:34,909 --> 00:00:36,911
"The Empty Boys: We're Gonna Smash It!"

15
00:00:36,995 --> 00:00:40,123
I stumbled on it while looking
at a channel run by my college friends!

16
00:00:40,206 --> 00:00:41,916
This guy isn't bad…

17
00:00:42,709 --> 00:00:45,837
You know, he might actually
be pretty interesting.

18
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,922
WE SPOKE TO SUCCESSFUL BUSINESSMAN
KONTA HOSHINO!

19
00:00:51,885 --> 00:00:53,970
What? I didn't get picked?

20
00:00:54,054 --> 00:00:55,805
You didn't. Too bad.

21
00:00:55,889 --> 00:01:00,268
But wasn't the role mine already,
and the audition was just a formality?

22
00:01:00,351 --> 00:01:02,020
That's what I heard.

23
00:01:02,103 --> 00:01:05,440
But Konta, you added your own lines
in the audition without permission.

24
00:01:05,523 --> 00:01:07,692
What? Right, I did do that.

25
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:10,862
<i>You turned two lines of dialogue</i>
<i>into about eight lines?</i>

26
00:01:10,945 --> 00:01:14,032
Oh, eight lines?
Did I talk that much? Yeah…

27
00:01:14,616 --> 00:01:16,451
That's why you didn't get picked!

28
00:01:16,534 --> 00:01:17,577
What?

29
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:21,331
I was acting straight from the soul,
and I just happened to speak eight lines!

30
00:01:21,915 --> 00:01:23,833
Listen here, Konta.

31
00:01:23,917 --> 00:01:28,630
An audition is where you show what you've
got, with the few lines you're given!

32
00:01:28,713 --> 00:01:31,382
The heck is that?

33
00:01:32,383 --> 00:01:34,677
And I was so confident about it too.

34
00:01:43,311 --> 00:01:45,563
Konta, what's for dinner toni--

35
00:01:48,066 --> 00:01:49,109
What's wrong?

36
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:58,284
Konta seems kind of depressed.

37
00:01:58,910 --> 00:02:01,663
The slumped back of an unemployed man.

38
00:02:02,288 --> 00:02:03,665
Oh, wait, we're unemployed too.

39
00:02:04,541 --> 00:02:06,543
Is he going to be okay?

40
00:02:15,385 --> 00:02:17,679
Hey, did something happen to Konta?

41
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:20,223
He's over there alone, looking all sad.

42
00:02:21,599 --> 00:02:22,767
I knew it.

43
00:02:22,851 --> 00:02:24,310
Huh? What do you mean?

44
00:02:24,394 --> 00:02:27,438
I bet he failed another audition.

45
00:02:28,606 --> 00:02:31,776
Whenever he fails an audition,
he listens to Fun-Mon.

46
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:33,111
Funky Monkey Babys?

47
00:02:33,194 --> 00:02:35,822
Yeah. Apparently,
it helps him feel better.

48
00:02:35,905 --> 00:02:39,909
But is he really all right?
From behind, he looks totally defeated.

49
00:02:39,993 --> 00:02:41,452
Well, he'll be fine.

50
00:02:41,536 --> 00:02:43,371
He'll be back to usual soon enough.

51
00:02:43,997 --> 00:02:46,374
-The power of Fun-Mon is amazing.
-Right?

52
00:02:54,966 --> 00:02:56,301
What?

53
00:02:56,384 --> 00:02:58,344
Am I getting scolded again?

54
00:02:58,428 --> 00:03:01,055
MANAGER

55
00:03:03,016 --> 00:03:04,309
Yes, hello?

56
00:03:05,643 --> 00:03:06,686
What?

57
00:03:07,645 --> 00:03:08,771
A documentary?

58
00:03:11,065 --> 00:03:12,150
On me?

59
00:03:50,021 --> 00:03:51,606
He's back.

60
00:03:51,689 --> 00:03:54,150
Konta, we started eating dinner.

61
00:03:58,947 --> 00:04:00,365
Want some beer?

62
00:04:00,448 --> 00:04:01,658
No, I'm good.

63
00:04:02,533 --> 00:04:03,743
I'll have barley tea.

64
00:04:05,870 --> 00:04:07,705
Isn't he kind of gloomy?

65
00:04:07,789 --> 00:04:09,457
Did Fun-Mon have no effect?

66
00:04:36,234 --> 00:04:37,485
Thanks for the food.

67
00:04:50,665 --> 00:04:51,916
Hey.

68
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:57,297
Do you know a show called
<i>Document Memoreal</i>?

69
00:05:00,174 --> 00:05:01,592
Huh? Yeah.

70
00:05:01,676 --> 00:05:03,011
I know it.

71
00:05:03,094 --> 00:05:05,054
It's that famous
day-in-the-life show, right?

72
00:05:05,138 --> 00:05:06,139
Yeah.

73
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:11,602
That show called and said
they want to do a feature on me.

74
00:05:12,186 --> 00:05:13,688
Say what?

75
00:05:13,771 --> 00:05:15,023
Yeah.

76
00:05:15,106 --> 00:05:17,483
Come on, what a lame lie.

77
00:05:17,567 --> 00:05:18,860
No, I'm serious.

78
00:05:18,943 --> 00:05:21,654
No, there's no way that's true! Right?

79
00:05:22,864 --> 00:05:24,032
You're being tricked.

80
00:05:24,115 --> 00:05:26,909
No, really. My manager
just called me a moment ago.

81
00:05:26,993 --> 00:05:29,078
He said they want to film
my life as an actor.

82
00:05:29,162 --> 00:05:31,456
Wait, seriously? Why?

83
00:05:31,539 --> 00:05:33,374
Is it really that unbelievable?

84
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:35,376
Yeah, I mean, you aren't successful.

85
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:37,462
Your fame as an actor is basically zero.

86
00:05:38,671 --> 00:05:42,383
Why did they even have the idea
to make you an offer in the first place?

87
00:05:42,467 --> 00:05:46,220
Apparently, their staff
saw the video those boys made

88
00:05:47,055 --> 00:05:48,973
the other day.

89
00:05:49,057 --> 00:05:51,267
-Huh?
-The video?

90
00:05:52,727 --> 00:05:53,561
This one?

91
00:05:53,644 --> 00:05:54,896
Yes, that one.

92
00:05:54,979 --> 00:05:58,775
Supposedly, the name "Empty Boys"
caught on, and it went a bit viral.

93
00:05:59,859 --> 00:06:02,820
Wait. So they saw this and made an offer?

94
00:06:02,904 --> 00:06:03,780
Yes.

95
00:06:04,530 --> 00:06:06,324
What a strange world.

96
00:06:06,407 --> 00:06:07,492
Wait.

97
00:06:07,575 --> 00:06:09,744
But if it's true, isn't this amazing?

98
00:06:09,827 --> 00:06:13,206
I'm telling you, it's true.
They saw this and sent me an offer!

99
00:06:13,289 --> 00:06:14,749
No way!

100
00:06:14,832 --> 00:06:16,125
That's awesome!

101
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:18,044
He'll be a documentary actor.

102
00:06:18,127 --> 00:06:19,545
You did it!

103
00:06:19,629 --> 00:06:21,798
I guess so, but…

104
00:06:22,381 --> 00:06:23,216
What?

105
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:27,053
What's with that attitude?

106
00:06:27,136 --> 00:06:29,222
Well, you see, I'm thinking

107
00:06:30,139 --> 00:06:31,682
maybe I'll turn it down.

108
00:06:32,391 --> 00:06:33,559
Seriously?

109
00:06:33,643 --> 00:06:35,728
Why?! This is a huge opportunity!

110
00:06:35,812 --> 00:06:37,355
It is, but…

111
00:06:37,438 --> 00:06:39,232
What? What is it?

112
00:06:39,315 --> 00:06:44,195
Listen, a day-in-the-life feature means
they'll film my private life, right?

113
00:06:44,278 --> 00:06:45,822
Well, of course they will.

114
00:06:46,405 --> 00:06:48,699
How is that going to turn out?

115
00:06:48,783 --> 00:06:50,243
Huh? Is there a problem?

116
00:06:50,326 --> 00:06:51,869
There is!

117
00:06:51,953 --> 00:06:55,331
Actors are supposed to keep
their private lives a mystery!

118
00:06:56,082 --> 00:06:59,418
Through our roles,
we speak to the audience's emotions!

119
00:06:59,502 --> 00:07:03,589
If my private life is shown too…

120
00:07:04,549 --> 00:07:05,883
It just takes away from it.

121
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:10,179
That's exactly
why I don't do social media.

122
00:07:10,263 --> 00:07:13,641
Koji Yakusho, my idol,
doesn't use it either. He's so mysterious.

123
00:07:13,724 --> 00:07:15,852
Well, of course,
Koji Yakusho wouldn't use it.

124
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:17,770
Konta.

125
00:07:17,854 --> 00:07:19,439
-Yeah?
-I'm sorry.

126
00:07:20,231 --> 00:07:21,941
As your younger sister,

127
00:07:22,608 --> 00:07:24,861
I'm just going to go ahead and say it.

128
00:07:24,944 --> 00:07:26,028
What?

129
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:30,533
You can't afford
to have such picky standards!

130
00:07:30,616 --> 00:07:31,659
Whoa.

131
00:07:31,742 --> 00:07:37,331
Building your recognition and getting work
is the most important thing, isn't it?

132
00:07:37,415 --> 00:07:41,294
Right? Literally nobody knows
you even exist right now.

133
00:07:41,377 --> 00:07:43,212
-Exist?
-Yeah. And!

134
00:07:43,296 --> 00:07:47,341
You're "mysterious" in the sense
that you don't even exist in the industry.

135
00:07:47,425 --> 00:07:48,301
Mysterious?

136
00:07:48,384 --> 00:07:51,888
Listen! You need to let people know
who Konta Hoshino even is!

137
00:07:51,971 --> 00:07:54,599
To that end,
refusing jobs is out of the question!

138
00:07:55,808 --> 00:07:57,560
Is that so?

139
00:07:57,643 --> 00:07:58,895
Yes, it is.

140
00:08:06,694 --> 00:08:07,862
Then…

141
00:08:09,489 --> 00:08:10,364
I'll do it.

142
00:08:10,448 --> 00:08:11,699
What did you say?

143
00:08:13,576 --> 00:08:16,078
This <i>Document Memoreal </i>job…

144
00:08:18,539 --> 00:08:19,916
I guess I'll take it!

145
00:08:33,012 --> 00:08:35,515
Sorry for making you help out
with the cleaning.

146
00:08:35,598 --> 00:08:38,309
It's fine. Let's make it
look nice for the shoot.

147
00:08:38,392 --> 00:08:39,560
Thanks.

148
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:43,773
Konta, did you not sleep?

149
00:08:43,856 --> 00:08:46,692
As a reference for today's show,

150
00:08:46,776 --> 00:08:49,862
I was binge-watching documentaries
on famous actors.

151
00:08:49,946 --> 00:08:51,030
I see.

152
00:08:51,113 --> 00:08:53,157
That doesn't sound good.

153
00:09:00,665 --> 00:09:01,624
Hup.

154
00:09:05,795 --> 00:09:07,421
Let me carry that.

155
00:09:08,047 --> 00:09:09,215
Mr. Nishigami.

156
00:09:10,216 --> 00:09:11,592
Thank you very much.

157
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:14,762
Cleaning the villa?

158
00:09:14,845 --> 00:09:16,264
Oh, yes.

159
00:09:16,347 --> 00:09:19,058
My brother is going to be
in a day-in-the-life feature.

160
00:09:19,141 --> 00:09:20,226
Day-in-the-life?

161
00:09:20,309 --> 00:09:23,145
So we have to clean up the villa.

162
00:09:23,229 --> 00:09:26,983
So, for this show, is someone coming over?

163
00:09:27,483 --> 00:09:30,861
Just the director.
Seems he is coming alone with a camera.

164
00:09:30,945 --> 00:09:35,241
Oh, but we'll make sure
not to cause you any inconvenience.

165
00:09:36,075 --> 00:09:39,620
How long will they be staying?

166
00:09:39,704 --> 00:09:42,290
I heard it will be about three days.

167
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:46,002
Still, I'm very worried.

168
00:09:46,085 --> 00:09:47,378
I see.

169
00:09:48,754 --> 00:09:52,300
But I'm happy for Mr. Konta.

170
00:09:59,432 --> 00:10:03,394
Wow, it's so clean now!
Rinrin, Tsumugi, thank you.

171
00:10:03,477 --> 00:10:04,604
You're welcome.

172
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:06,188
Hey!

173
00:10:07,607 --> 00:10:10,318
What do you think about my clothes?

174
00:10:10,985 --> 00:10:13,779
Huh? Do you plan
to be on the show like that?

175
00:10:13,863 --> 00:10:14,822
Well, yeah.

176
00:10:14,905 --> 00:10:16,365
Absolutely don't do that!

177
00:10:16,449 --> 00:10:20,453
Really? Wait, don't I look sharp in this?

178
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:23,539
You're so uncool.

179
00:10:23,623 --> 00:10:25,541
Promise me you won't wear that outfit.

180
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:28,586
Oh, really?
I think it looks awesome, though.

181
00:10:31,422 --> 00:10:34,175
All right!
To get ready for the shoot tomorrow,

182
00:10:34,258 --> 00:10:37,261
Tetsuro, could you give my face
a massage to slim it down?

183
00:10:37,345 --> 00:10:39,221
I've never done anything like that before.

184
00:10:39,305 --> 00:10:42,183
It's fine. Just search,
"Slimming face massage,"

185
00:10:42,266 --> 00:10:44,143
"How to do," and you'll get it.

186
00:10:44,226 --> 00:10:46,145
-Do it! Let's go.
-Okay, I'll look it up.

187
00:10:46,228 --> 00:10:48,981
Don't leave me behind.
Hey, don't leave the star behind!

188
00:10:49,065 --> 00:10:51,233
Which way am I supposed to go? Straight?

189
00:10:51,317 --> 00:10:53,027
Watch out, there's a step.

190
00:10:53,110 --> 00:10:56,280
Why are you saying that yourself?
Hey, there's a huge step again.

191
00:10:56,364 --> 00:10:58,157
Konta is really getting cocky.

192
00:10:58,240 --> 00:11:00,826
Just yesterday, he was wondering
whether he should accept it.

193
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:01,744
Yeah.

194
00:11:01,827 --> 00:11:06,332
He definitely thinks he'll go viral
and become popular after the show.

195
00:11:06,957 --> 00:11:08,876
I wonder if things
will really go that well.

196
00:11:14,048 --> 00:11:15,257
Good morning.

197
00:11:15,341 --> 00:11:17,343
Hello.

198
00:11:18,010 --> 00:11:20,721
Good morning.
I'm Torihara from <i>Document Memoreal</i>.

199
00:11:22,181 --> 00:11:24,225
I'm the actor, Konta… Wait.

200
00:11:25,434 --> 00:11:27,478
I'm the actor…

201
00:11:27,561 --> 00:11:29,397
Konta Hoshino.

202
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:30,731
Thank you very much.

203
00:11:33,317 --> 00:11:36,195
This is the schedule we have planned.

204
00:11:40,324 --> 00:11:42,701
Has the narrator been decided yet?

205
00:11:42,785 --> 00:11:44,328
Oh, not yet.

206
00:11:44,412 --> 00:11:47,081
Then please get Koji Yakusho.

207
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:50,418
No, I don't think we can…

208
00:11:50,501 --> 00:11:52,545
Just ask him, just in case.

209
00:11:52,628 --> 00:11:56,507
Narration is very important
for a documentary. Get someone good!

210
00:11:57,091 --> 00:12:00,219
For now, shall we start shooting
the villa's exterior?

211
00:12:00,302 --> 00:12:01,512
-All right.
-Let's do it.

212
00:12:01,595 --> 00:12:03,097
Midori, guide him.

213
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:04,974
Okay. This way.

214
00:12:05,057 --> 00:12:06,475
Thank you very much.

215
00:12:08,102 --> 00:12:09,770
Are you a family member?

216
00:12:09,854 --> 00:12:11,480
Well, he's my older brother.

217
00:12:11,564 --> 00:12:12,815
-Oh, I see.
-Yeah.

218
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:14,733
I would like to interview you later.

219
00:12:18,154 --> 00:12:21,282
Hello? Mr. Torihara is already here.

220
00:12:21,365 --> 00:12:22,867
<i>Oh, sorry.</i>

221
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:26,036
<i>I'm at a different set now,</i>
<i>I don't have time to head over there.</i>

222
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:27,913
<i>You'll be fine on your own, right?</i>

223
00:12:27,997 --> 00:12:30,374
What? Seriously?

224
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:33,252
How can I look professional
if my manager isn't here?

225
00:12:33,335 --> 00:12:35,004
Come on!

226
00:12:36,755 --> 00:12:39,717
What should I do? A manager…

227
00:12:40,342 --> 00:12:43,471
This is a really magnificent villa.

228
00:12:44,013 --> 00:12:46,223
It's actually my grandmother's place.

229
00:12:47,349 --> 00:12:50,978
Mr. Torihara,
please take good care of my brother.

230
00:12:51,061 --> 00:12:51,979
What?

231
00:12:52,062 --> 00:12:55,232
To be honest, he is an idiot,

232
00:12:55,316 --> 00:12:59,403
but he works really hard
to get acting jobs.

233
00:12:59,487 --> 00:13:01,030
Leave it to me.

234
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:04,241
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

235
00:13:04,325 --> 00:13:06,911
Nice to meet you.

236
00:13:06,994 --> 00:13:09,205
Why those outfits and make-up?

237
00:13:09,288 --> 00:13:10,873
We thought we might be on camera too.

238
00:13:10,956 --> 00:13:13,459
Men may see us and think,
"Who is that girl?"

239
00:13:13,542 --> 00:13:15,127
And contact us!

240
00:13:15,211 --> 00:13:16,754
-That sounds good.
-Good?

241
00:13:16,837 --> 00:13:19,965
What exactly are you expecting
from my brother's show?

242
00:13:20,049 --> 00:13:21,342
It's a possibility.

243
00:13:21,425 --> 00:13:22,843
Hello.

244
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:26,013
-Nice to meet you.
-This is my manager.

245
00:13:26,096 --> 00:13:26,972
-What?
-Konta…

246
00:13:27,056 --> 00:13:28,182
Just play along.

247
00:13:28,265 --> 00:13:31,519
Hello, I am Director Torihara.

248
00:13:32,311 --> 00:13:34,980
I am Konta Hoshino's manager.

249
00:13:35,064 --> 00:13:36,398
-Well then, everyone…
-Sorry.

250
00:13:36,482 --> 00:13:38,692
I look forward to working with you all!

251
00:13:38,776 --> 00:13:40,110
The pleasure is ours!

252
00:13:40,194 --> 00:13:41,111
Thank you.

253
00:13:50,829 --> 00:13:55,209
That villa attracts
one human after another.

254
00:14:04,176 --> 00:14:09,014
I could never have imagined
you were the mastermind all along.

255
00:14:10,975 --> 00:14:13,644
Yes, that's a wrap for this cut.

256
00:14:13,727 --> 00:14:16,146
Wow, that was wonderful.

257
00:14:16,230 --> 00:14:18,399
May I ask a few questions?

258
00:14:18,482 --> 00:14:21,652
I truly think you are
a one-of-a-kind actor, Konta.

259
00:14:21,735 --> 00:14:22,945
One-of-a-kind, yes.

260
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:25,489
Are there any actors
you take inspiration from?

261
00:14:25,573 --> 00:14:26,949
Well…

262
00:14:27,032 --> 00:14:28,200
DiCaprio, I suppose.

263
00:14:28,284 --> 00:14:29,493
DiCap--

264
00:14:29,577 --> 00:14:32,329
I feel a sort of connection with him.

265
00:14:32,413 --> 00:14:36,292
He has the same eyes as me.

266
00:14:37,585 --> 00:14:38,586
T-The same eyes?

267
00:14:38,669 --> 00:14:41,005
Oh, yes. The same eyes.

268
00:14:41,755 --> 00:14:44,592
Well, our facial features
are quite similar too.

269
00:14:44,675 --> 00:14:45,885
Of course,

270
00:14:45,968 --> 00:14:50,097
he is a Hollywood superstar,
but I plan on catching up to him.

271
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:53,559
Or rather, overtaking him,
so you could say he's my rival?

272
00:14:54,310 --> 00:14:56,270
Something like a rival, I guess.

273
00:14:57,313 --> 00:15:00,190
Interesting. May I ask one more question?

274
00:15:00,274 --> 00:15:02,276
Are you okay? Please drink some water.

275
00:15:02,359 --> 00:15:05,237
My throat is dry.
Your questions are coming too fast.

276
00:15:05,321 --> 00:15:06,572
Sorry, I got carried away.

277
00:15:06,655 --> 00:15:09,742
Is there anything you try
to be mindful of when acting?

278
00:15:09,825 --> 00:15:11,577
-Oh, actors…
-Yes.

279
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:16,290
When we act,
we live out the lives of many people.

280
00:15:16,373 --> 00:15:20,294
But, of course, I am also a person,
and I have a life of my own.

281
00:15:20,377 --> 00:15:23,839
So, in the moments
when I live another person's life,

282
00:15:23,923 --> 00:15:25,507
I sort of kill my own self.

283
00:15:25,591 --> 00:15:27,968
Or rather, it's like… How should I put it…

284
00:15:28,636 --> 00:15:29,762
How should I put it…

285
00:15:29,845 --> 00:15:32,473
-How do you put it?
-How should I put it…

286
00:15:37,937 --> 00:15:39,104
Bloodlust…

287
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:41,106
Who goes there?

288
00:15:46,528 --> 00:15:48,238
What? Who goes there?

289
00:15:59,917 --> 00:16:01,460
Come here!

290
00:16:02,127 --> 00:16:04,630
You come here! Come!

291
00:16:08,217 --> 00:16:09,927
Is he really going to be okay?

292
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:11,136
I don't know.

293
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:13,681
He might be getting a little carried away.

294
00:16:35,494 --> 00:16:37,746
For us actors,
our bodies are our greatest asset.

295
00:16:37,830 --> 00:16:38,831
You're amazing.

296
00:16:38,914 --> 00:16:40,749
Oh, that's great.

297
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:43,419
<i>It would be great</i>
<i>if this really makes Konta successful.</i>

298
00:16:43,502 --> 00:16:46,922
<i>It's like my brother has completely</i>
<i>changed since the show started.</i>

299
00:16:47,006 --> 00:16:48,882
I don't want people to find out I'm poor!

300
00:16:48,966 --> 00:16:50,050
It's actually good!

301
00:16:50,759 --> 00:16:51,802
<i>What a handsome man.</i>

302
00:16:51,885 --> 00:16:53,512
Please don't film that man.

303
00:16:53,595 --> 00:16:55,639
<i>Acting is my true calling.</i>

304
00:16:55,723 --> 00:16:57,933
I was born to act.

305
00:16:58,017 --> 00:16:59,727
<i>You are an example for all actors.</i>

306
00:16:59,810 --> 00:17:02,521
If we inflate his ego more,
we can film something way funnier.

307
00:17:02,604 --> 00:17:04,690
That's what the viewers are looking for.

308
00:17:04,773 --> 00:17:07,609
<i>Everyone is supporting me,</i>
<i>so I want to get on top,</i>

309
00:17:07,693 --> 00:17:09,361
for their sake.

310
00:17:10,571 --> 00:17:11,530
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
